entals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Nick LaLota (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Nick LaLota runs for reelection in a Long Island district that leans Republican by about four points. He enters the final weeks with a large financial advantage, having raised roughly $4.5 million to Chris Gallant's $1.7 million, and holds more than five times Gallant's cash on hand. Rating outlets split between Lean Republican and Likely Republican, with two calling the race Solid Republican, and prediction markets give Gallant about a one-in-four chance of winning.\n\nGallant, a gay Army Black Hawk pilot, drew wide attention after intimate photos went viral, and his fundraising rose following the episode; he has campaigned on affordability and his record of public service. The only available poll, conducted in December by a Democratic-leaning firm, showed LaLota ahead by three points. A favorable national climate for Democrats keeps the race competitive, but the incumbent's advantages and the district's lean make him the favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1953, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.158, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1553, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.188, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1399, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0851, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1487, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1542, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1035, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1186, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1205, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.124, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1216, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1197, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.084, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1405, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1018, "margi